  "implementation": [
    "Capture original first-import modern DXF variable raw bodies as private shared_ptr<const> baselines. Precharge a private container-lifetime logical allowance including map/control overhead before copying; failed raw-list insertion erases the inserted baseline and does not charge bytes. Existing public raw-callback counts remain unchanged; sticky capture failure blocks output.",
    "Generalize the custom modern snapshot/inspection path to standard and application variables, preserving canonical root and custom ownership admission. DWG typed output and legacy canonical raw replay remain distinct. No installed library headers, callbacks/pure virtuals or DWG byte parsers change; private dx_data/dx_iface users must recompile.",
    "Owning-decode original and current raw bodies in the original captured wire context. Reconcile schema and value independently against the immutable baseline: typed-only and raw-only changes compose, disjoint changes combine, identical same-field changes agree, and differing same-field changes refuse before publication. Require current common metadata to match its raw representation.",
    "Retain a unique DictionaryVariables body. Preserve omitted default fields and exact unchanged numeric spelling. Rewrite changed existing represented slots, insert changed omitted slots at the body boundary, and transcode existing known text across ASCII/Binary. Retain opaque fields from the current raw model. Ambiguous/repeated structural or represented slots refuse; unknown schema semantics are not invented.",
    "Precharge 64 times both current and original raw logical estimates plus twice typed logical storage before decoding/copying. This is bounded logical accounting, not a controlled RSS/performance result.",
    "Freeze current typed/raw sources, immutable baseline pointer, reconciled output schema/value and complete raw projection. Existing dictionary snapshots guard containing entries/owners. Revalidate identities/fields through callbacks and use actual output field/reference proof plus owning-decode before final publication.",
    "Move the allocating hasSingleSuccessfulNamedResourceImport check inside the noexcept preparation method try block. A persistent allocation-failure control previously aborted at the unguarded provenance check; direct LLDB evidence and corrected reached-failure/retry controls are retained.",
    "Add an optional C++ test probe that edits actual independently generated EZDXF_META data, then independent peer readback of edited text and preserved owners/material matrices/3D geometry. Use documented peer Unicode normalization once for both formats and caret normalization for ASCII only. No peer parser or drawing payload is copied into Git."
  ],
