    "profiles": "Four modern versions x two source formats x two output formats x standard/application owner. Each checks unchanged, typed value/schema, raw-only value, disjoint schema/value, agreeing edits, both conflict fields and corrected retries, plus an opaque raw-field edit with literal wire proof and owning readback.",
    "presence": "32 source/output/owner/presence profiles retain schema/value absence unchanged and insert both represented fields when edited. Two literal ASCII numeric spellings remain exact through a value edit.",
    "callbacks": "40 standard-route real callback mutations across four phases and both encodings: typed value, raw value, duplicate typed identity, duplicate raw identity and containing dictionary entry. Sentinel destinations and absence of owned temporary files are checked, then corrected same-adapter outputs pass.",
    "allocation": "20 sparse preparation offsets (0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256 per encoding) reach16 actual persistent allocation failures. All attempts retain sentinel destinations; all20 subsequent normal exports/readbacks succeed. These are direct preparation injections, not filesystem or exhaustive whole-export fault coverage.",
    "outputCorruption": "26 field corruptions of replayed completed standard-route edited OBJECTS views are refused by the actual inspector; restored views pass. Existing application-route view corruptions remain in the affected cohort.",
    "compatibility": "The cohort retains existing application ownership/refusal/retry profiles, canonical DXF/synthetic typed DWG value edits, dictionary owner/default/source tests, named-resource typed/raw limits, MATERIAL controls, local/installed CLI probes and LibreCAD_3 compile checks. These are not formal ABI/application or native Linux/Windows FreeCAD qualification."
